Author:     recky-c <ruiqicheng510@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Fri Oct 23 15:09:15 2026 +0800
Commit:     GitHub <noreply@github.com>
CommitDate: Fri Oct 23 15:09:15 2026 +0800

    [Refactor][MRV2][PCP] Pass PCP context through common attention metadata (#19331)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Pass `pcp_context` and `pcp_cache_group_idx` through
    `AscendCommonAttentionMetadata`. Update attention builders to read these
    fields and remove PCP-specific argument forwarding, capability markers,
    and forwarding-only capture overrides.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    NPU comparisons matched tokens and logprobs for completed GQA, MLA/MTP,
    and SFA cases. DSA/V4.1 runs completed but did not establish strict
    numerical equivalence.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: recky-c <ruiqicheng510@gmail.com>
    Signed-off-by: chengruiqi (C) <c00913489@china.huawei.com>
    Co-authored-by: chengruiqi (C) <c00913489@china.huawei.com>

